{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>What</b> — It is known that the moon and the eleven stars are like a point on the sphere relative to the firmament, and the entire earth is like an indivisible point, and a human being is a divisible fraction that cannot receive a division relative to the entire earth. Therefore: <i>what is man that You should remember him</i> — in a disparaging sense. And the meaning: since You have great and honored creations beyond man, how did it come to mind to give him honor."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:26:38.065192040Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}